{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00332",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.97,
      "end_seconds": 3.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. Can I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.31,
      "end_seconds": 7.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.23,
      "end_seconds": 14.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Mainly I've been passing out once last week. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.46,
      "end_seconds": 21.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.09,
      "end_seconds": 33.33,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "It's been going on for about four days. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.04,
      "end_seconds": 41.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.03,
      "end_seconds": 60.81,
      "duration_seconds": 18.78,
      "text": "I mean, only lying down, and it's not much. I'd say all the time. Severe, I'd say. I notice it more with standing for long. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I had a bump on my head after before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.62,
      "end_seconds": 63.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.45,
      "end_seconds": 65.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.53,
      "end_seconds": 86.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Let me check a few things. Any shaking or jerking or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.14,
      "end_seconds": 91.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Hmm, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.42,
      "end_seconds": 96.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Right, any chest pain, tongue biting or loss of bladder control?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.11,
      "end_seconds": 100.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, um, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.2,
      "end_seconds": 104.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Go on. And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.87,
      "end_seconds": 108.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I mean, no, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.35,
      "end_seconds": 112.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.93,
      "end_seconds": 118.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.88,
      "end_seconds": 121.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.83,
      "end_seconds": 124.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.4,
      "end_seconds": 135.06,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Okay. Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.3,
      "end_seconds": 139.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.96,
      "end_seconds": 144.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.33,
      "end_seconds": 149.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I'm allergic to pollen, I get a runny nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.5,
      "end_seconds": 155.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Right, is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.0,
      "end_seconds": 158.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.48,
      "end_seconds": 162.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.16,
      "end_seconds": 171.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Yes, I had my tonsils out, when I was a child. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.83,
      "end_seconds": 179.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.8,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.37,
      "end_seconds": 193.82,
      "duration_seconds": 13.45,
      "text": "I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.4,
      "end_seconds": 198.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.12,
      "end_seconds": 201.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 202.77,
      "end_seconds": 210.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BP is 111 over 78, saturation 97 percent, temperature is 36.5 degrees, heart rate 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.74,
      "end_seconds": 216.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.66,
      "end_seconds": 229.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "I mean, um, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.39,
      "end_seconds": 236.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.3,
      "end_seconds": 238.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.3,
      "end_seconds": 241.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.37,
      "end_seconds": 260.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "No murmurs on listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.79,
      "end_seconds": 293.17,
      "duration_seconds": 26.38,
      "text": "Alright, all done, thank you, please sit down. From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like a simple faint, probably reflex-related. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep dehydration in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been passing out once last week for about four days, severe, and no chest pain or loss of bladder control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.98,
      "end_seconds": 295.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.74,
      "end_seconds": 315.54,
      "duration_seconds": 16.8,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood tests for syncope. Drink enough water and avoid standing still for long stretches, and sit if you feel it coming. If you pass out again, especially with chest pain or palpitations, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.55,
      "end_seconds": 322.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.2,
      "end_seconds": 325.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Come back in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.84,
      "end_seconds": 329.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Hmm, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.13,
      "end_seconds": 337.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.3,
      "end_seconds": 342.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "So, I come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.38,
      "end_seconds": 347.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.71,
      "end_seconds": 354.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}